  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Protection and Assistance of Venezuelan Migrants victims of trafficking - Phase II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As the lead agency of Quito Process Trafficking and Smuggling Working Group, IOM has committed to providing technical and financial support for the Prevention and Prosecution of the crime of Trafficking in Persons, as well as the protection and assistance to its victims; and to coordinating the required actions for the implementation of international cooperation projects in this area, as identified by the Group of Friends of the Quito Process and in alignment with the needs and priorities of the Quito Process member states.Therefore, IOM will continue the efforts implemented in the first phase of the &#x201c;Protection and Assistance to Venezuelan Migrants Victims of Trafficking&#x201d; project, to improve regional response capacities and protection services for Venezuelan victims of trafficking and for those at risk of becoming victims. The project&#x2019;s second phase will continue to improve the capacities of relevant stakeholders and institutions in the region to provide a counter-trafficking response. The outputs aim to provide the needed technical support for member states to achieve the proposed actions established by the Regional Coordination Mechanism of the Quito Process as well as expand VoTs&#x2019; access to protection-related and assistance services.</narrative>
  </description>
